284
00:14:50,799 --> 00:14:52,559
I saw you go to property management today.

285
00:14:56,340 --> 00:14:57,519
Just paying the property management fee.

286
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,559
Pay for a year, get half a year free.

287
00:15:05,659 --> 00:15:06,600
Aren't you going in?

288
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:20,320
Laicai.

289
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:21,360
Stop barking. Let's go.

290
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:22,200
Come on.

291
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,879
Didn't I tell you to watch the pot?

292
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:44,320
Do you just not hear a word I say?

293
00:15:44,679 --> 00:15:46,240
I wasn't just sitting around either!

294
00:15:54,139 --> 00:15:54,879
Wait a minute.

295
00:16:13,879 --> 00:16:15,360
Have you met the neighbor on the second floor?

296
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:18,100
The neighbor on the second floor?

297
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:20,960
No, I haven't. No idea.

298
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,539
You've lived here alone for almost half a year.

299
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:24,120
How come you don't know anything?

300
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:26,039
Property management told me today

301
00:16:26,259 --> 00:16:28,320
that Wan Fenqi's wife from across the hall went missing.

302
00:16:28,639 --> 00:16:29,620
The police even showed up.

303
00:16:29,659 --> 00:16:30,600
You didn't know about this either?

304
00:16:31,659 --> 00:16:32,500
That's ginger.

305
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:34,720
That's the second piece. Can't you taste it?

306
00:16:38,799 --> 00:16:39,639
At our hospital,

307
00:16:40,919 --> 00:16:42,159
we recently admitted a patient.

308
00:16:42,259 --> 00:16:43,320
Brought in with a heart attack.

309
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:46,480
His wife was slumped over his bed,

310
00:16:47,639 --> 00:16:49,000
crying her eyes out.

311
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:50,620
And do you know

312
00:16:50,899 --> 00:16:51,639
when that guy woke up,

313
00:16:51,679 --> 00:16:52,960
what his first words were?

314
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:53,879
What did he say?

315
00:16:54,019 --> 00:16:55,080
He said, "Honey...

316
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,679
Received.

317
00:16:58,259 --> 00:16:59,720
I'll send it to you in a bit."

318
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:02,360
Isn't that crazy?

319
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:04,440
What job is more important than your life?

320
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:05,920
He probably didn't actually think

321
00:17:06,019 --> 00:17:07,380
that his job was so important.

322
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:08,779
He might have felt that

323
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:11,079
if he couldn't pay his mortgage

324
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,279
and lost his home,

325
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,400
it might actually be

326
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,160
more... more important than his own life.

327
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:25,359
If you can't tell a joke to cheer someone up, don't.

328
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,640
It's not funny at all.

329
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,420
Ma Du

330
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,319
Ma Du

331
00:17:56,039 --> 00:17:57,559
Ma Du, can you hear me?

332
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:58,720
Can you hear me?

333
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:05,400
Ma...

334
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:08,579
Where did you go?

335
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,839
I... um...

336
00:18:11,039 --> 00:18:12,140
I... I'm at the hospital.

337
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,039
There was an emergency in the ward,

338
00:18:13,039 --> 00:18:14,160
so I was called back.

339
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,279
What's wrong?

340
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:17,920
Come back right now.

341
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,039
I just saw someone outside the window.

342
00:18:20,299 --> 00:18:20,759
Just...

343
00:18:20,819 --> 00:18:22,480
In our yard... I...

344
00:18:23,299 --> 00:18:23,700
Listen,

345
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,339
I'm heading home right now.

346
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,599
Stop scaring yourself.

347
00:18:42,839 --> 00:18:44,259
You took my package by mistake again.

348
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,799
Can I come in and take a look?

349
00:18:48,079 --> 00:18:48,920
Ma Du

350
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:51,000
Go see what's going on.

351
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,240
He's not here.

352
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:53,839
I know.

353
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:02,799
What exactly do you want?

354
00:19:03,099 --> 00:19:04,519
If you don't leave, I'm calling the police.

355
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:26,720
Verification failed

356
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,160
Verification failed

357
00:19:28,519 --> 00:19:29,539
Verification failed

358
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:31,759
Welcome home

359
00:19:31,759 --> 00:19:32,559
Tingting

360
00:19:33,519 --> 00:19:34,279
What's wrong?

361
00:19:34,819 --> 00:19:35,940
I was out earlier.

362
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:37,680
I couldn't hear clearly on the phone.

363
00:19:38,599 --> 00:19:39,359
What happened?

364
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:41,240
It's okay, it's okay. I'm back.

365
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,000
He... he was pressed against the window.

366
00:19:43,059 --> 00:19:43,839
Who? Who was peeping?

367
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,039
The... the guy from across the hall.

368
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,519
And he kept ringing the doorbell.

369
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:50,539
Saying something about grabbing the wrong package.

370
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:51,680
He insisted on coming in.

371
00:19:52,079 --> 00:19:53,680
It's... it's okay now. It's okay.

372
00:19:53,779 --> 00:19:55,480
He even insisted you weren't home.

373
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:57,960
How did he know you weren't home?

374
00:19:58,660 --> 00:20:00,440
Has he been spying on us?

375
00:20:01,559 --> 00:20:02,839
No, I need to call the police.

376
00:20:03,279 --> 00:20:03,960
Tingting.

377
00:20:05,019 --> 00:20:06,839
We don't need to call the police over this.

378
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,559
He probably just took the wrong package.

379
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:10,799
Look, just calm down a bit.

380
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,920
Am... am I not calm?

381
00:20:15,579 --> 00:20:16,859
His wife is missing.

382
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:18,559
The police even showed up at his door.

383
00:20:19,839 --> 00:20:20,480
That guy...

384
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:22,319
Wan Fenqi.

385
00:20:22,779 --> 00:20:24,359
There's really something wrong with him.

386
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:26,160
You know me.

387
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:28,839
Am I the type to panic over nothing?

388
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:33,799
Tell you what, Tingting.

389
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:36,500
I'll go talk to my colleagues in psych tomorrow.

390
00:20:36,539 --> 00:20:37,559
We'll get you some medication.

391
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:39,880
That way you can sleep a bit better at night.

392
00:20:42,859 --> 00:20:43,799
No, Ma Du.

393
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:46,000
Do you really think I have postpartum anxiety,

394
00:20:46,539 --> 00:20:47,400
or are you just doing your usual trick,

395
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:48,380
sweeping everything under the rug?

396
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:49,220
No, Tingting, I didn't mean...

397
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:51,240
Can you not act like a turtle

398
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,400
hiding in its shell?

399
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:53,059
I swear...

400
00:20:53,059 --> 00:20:53,900
If we don't resolve this,

401
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:55,440
it will only get more dangerous.

402
00:20:55,799 --> 00:20:57,200
We still need to bring the baby back later.

403
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:58,279
Have you even thought about that?

404
00:20:58,359 --> 00:20:59,259
Can you, at a time like this,

405
00:20:59,259 --> 00:21:00,759
step up like a man?

406
00:21:05,039 --> 00:21:05,720
Mom.

407
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,640
It's okay, it's okay. Ma Du is back.

408
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,200
You go back to sleep.

409
00:21:28,759 --> 00:21:30,240
I was so mad at the time.

410
00:21:30,599 --> 00:21:31,400
I swallowed my anger.

411
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:32,799
It wasn't because I felt sorry for him.

412
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:33,920
I was just thinking

413
00:21:34,279 --> 00:21:35,880
that my coupon was about to expire,

414
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,619
and I had to get up early to grab groceries.

415
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:39,359
When I got back to the bedroom,

416
00:21:39,599 --> 00:21:40,640
I was too mad to sleep.

417
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:41,759
So I scrolled on my phone

418
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:43,559
and bought three dresses at once.

419
00:21:44,059 --> 00:21:45,480
I thought, why am I saving money for him?

420
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:46,759
I'm a mental patient anyway.

421
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:51,160
But when I woke up this morning,

422
00:21:51,519 --> 00:21:52,480
I canceled the orders.

423
00:21:53,799 --> 00:21:55,000
What else can I do but save?

424
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:56,700
You can't save much on the small things.

425
00:21:56,759 --> 00:21:58,200
You have to focus on the big expenses.

426
00:21:58,859 --> 00:21:59,700
I advised you back then,

427
00:21:59,740 --> 00:22:01,319
not to rush into buying a house. Just wait.

428
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:02,200
But look what happened.

429
00:22:03,059 --> 00:22:04,440
It's not that bad.

430
00:22:04,779 --> 00:22:05,859
No, it's not.

431
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:07,259
Prices downtown are dropping,

432
00:22:07,339 --> 00:22:08,359
let alone in your area.

433
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:09,119
Look at me,

434
00:22:09,259 --> 00:22:10,200
I'm just saving my money.

435
00:22:10,339 --> 00:22:11,440
I'll wait for prices to drop by a down payment,

436
00:22:11,539 --> 00:22:12,559
before I consider buying.

437
00:22:20,759 --> 00:22:22,119
I need to run back home real quick.

438
00:22:22,380 --> 00:22:23,960
My laundry is going to get soaked.

439
00:22:24,059 --> 00:22:24,640
Hurry back then.

440
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:25,920
You don't have a shift this afternoon anyway.

441
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:27,839
I'll get going.

442
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,799
I had the security guard check the footage for you.

443
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:22,799
The window did shatter on its own.

444
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:25,000
We submitted a repair request a long time ago.

445
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:26,759
Can it be fixed right away today?

446
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:28,259
I can only say as soon as possible.

447
00:23:28,519 --> 00:23:30,480
It really depends on the developer's schedule.

448
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:31,779
By the way,

449
00:23:31,819 --> 00:23:33,440
you can pay the property management fee now.

450
00:23:33,559 --> 00:23:34,000
You...

451
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:12,279
Please take a look here.

452
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:14,440
Right this way.

453
00:24:15,759 --> 00:24:17,160
Every study in this building

454
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:19,000
has a fire escape door

455
00:24:19,339 --> 00:24:20,400
leading to the stairwell.

456
00:24:20,579 --> 00:24:22,279
It's one of our special features.

457
00:24:22,940 --> 00:24:24,039
But as for this side door...

458
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:25,519
we advise against using it regularly.

459
00:24:26,380 --> 00:24:27,460
I feel like later on, with the baby,

460
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:28,960
playing hide-and-seek here would be fun.

461
00:24:30,579 --> 00:24:32,440
Let me show you the outdoor yard next.

462
00:24:32,539 --> 00:24:33,480
Come, over here.

463
00:25:24,359 --> 00:25:25,039
What are you doing?!

464
00:25:27,839 --> 00:25:28,480
Listen to me...

465
00:25:29,180 --> 00:25:29,960
Don't move!

466
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:31,359
Don't move!

467
00:25:33,119 --> 00:25:34,640
Listen to me, let me explain!

468
00:25:36,299 --> 00:25:36,960
Don't move!

469
00:25:37,119 --> 00:25:38,079
I've already called the police!

470
00:25:38,980 --> 00:25:40,480
No! Don't call the police!

471
00:25:40,660 --> 00:25:41,680
No! No!

472
00:25:53,380 --> 00:25:56,920
I'm really out of options.

473
00:26:02,079 --> 00:26:03,799
I can't find my wife.

474
00:26:05,160 --> 00:26:06,920
If I wasn't so desperate,

475
00:26:07,559 --> 00:26:09,759
I wouldn't be doing this.

476
00:26:10,779 --> 00:26:12,839
Do you hear yourself right now?

477
00:26:13,319 --> 00:26:14,700
You're in my house,

478
00:26:15,319 --> 00:26:16,720
looking for your wife.

479
00:26:23,079 --> 00:26:24,039
Stop crying.

480
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:25,079
Pull yourself together.

481
00:26:25,279 --> 00:26:26,279
Look me in the eye.

482
00:26:31,779 --> 00:26:33,000
I'm trying to say,

483
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:36,599
your husband

484
00:26:38,019 --> 00:26:40,039
is hiding my wife.

485
00:26:43,079 --> 00:26:44,119
My husband

486
00:26:44,359 --> 00:26:46,519
is so busy I don't even see him.

487
00:26:47,079 --> 00:26:49,240
And he has time to hide your wife?

488
00:26:54,039 --> 00:26:55,240
What I mean is,

489
00:26:56,599 --> 00:26:57,519
my wife

490
00:26:58,640 --> 00:27:00,339
was kidnapped by your husband.

491
00:27:01,180 --> 00:27:02,279
A lot of things

492
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:04,160
aren't what they seem.

493
00:27:04,660 --> 00:27:06,079
Just hear me out.

494
00:27:14,220 --> 00:27:15,880
I dare you to say that again.

495
00:27:16,099 --> 00:27:17,960
It'll be the same however many times I say it.

496
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:20,200
Your major fortune cycle has ended.

497
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:23,279
From now on, you'll only sink deeper.

498
00:27:23,420 --> 00:27:25,279
You brought this on yourself.

499
00:27:25,519 --> 00:27:27,400
This is your fate.

500
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:31,839
The CRB Index just collapsed!

501
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:32,900
Within 15 minutes,

502
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:34,519
close all related positions!

503
00:27:34,579 --> 00:27:35,839
Whatever the price, whatever the reason.

504
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:37,319
I want zero risk exposure.

505
00:27:37,859 --> 00:27:39,839
Hurry up! Start making calls!

506
00:27:40,019 --> 00:27:41,039
Liquidate them all!

507
00:27:41,180 --> 00:27:42,319
I'll say it one more time.

508
00:27:42,519 --> 00:27:43,779
Whoever is the last to liquidate

509
00:27:43,960 --> 00:27:45,759
can go explain to Risk Control themselves

510
00:27:45,900 --> 00:27:47,319
why their bonus is zero this year.

511
00:27:47,319 --> 00:27:48,839
Right, right, we're already clearing them!

512
00:27:48,940 --> 00:27:49,859
In this situation,

513
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:51,119
we must pull out first to avoid the

514
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:52,599
risk.

515
00:27:53,759 --> 00:27:54,599
Don't leave a single share.

516
00:27:59,880 --> 00:28:00,680
What are you doing?

517
00:28:01,619 --> 00:28:03,000
Liquidate all positions! Didn't you hear?

518
00:28:03,059 --> 00:28:03,920
I heard him.

519
00:28:04,359 --> 00:28:05,299
He's being an idiot.

520
00:28:05,359 --> 00:28:06,799
Why should I do the same?

521
00:28:06,839 --> 00:28:08,160
It's not about who's being an idiot right now.

522
00:28:13,140 --> 00:28:14,759
What are you doing? Are you deaf?

523
00:28:15,460 --> 00:28:16,759
The fundamentals haven't changed.

524
00:28:16,920 --> 00:28:18,160
It's just sentiment that's changed.

525
00:28:18,339 --> 00:28:19,519
At this price,

526
00:28:19,799 --> 00:28:21,400
the market is basically giving away free money.

527
00:28:21,559 --> 00:28:23,759
I'm telling you to liquidate everything right now!

528
00:28:34,259 --> 00:28:35,559
I added another 500 lots.

529
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:36,640
Don't panic.

530
00:28:36,859 --> 00:28:38,759
I'm using my own risk limit.

531
00:28:38,839 --> 00:28:39,319
You...

532
00:28:39,460 --> 00:28:40,839
You're gambling!

533
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:42,599
I'm warning you one last time.

534
00:28:42,779 --> 00:28:43,799
Either liquidate it now,

535
00:28:43,839 --> 00:28:45,000
or get the hell out of here.

536
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:52,119
You...

537
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:53,359
Boss, boss, calm down.

538
00:28:53,359 --> 00:28:54,640
Go, go, call security.

539
00:28:54,759 --> 00:28:55,880
Get security over here!

540
00:28:57,599 --> 00:28:58,279
Boss.

541
00:28:59,980 --> 00:29:00,680
It went up!

542
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,400
Unbelievable.

543
00:29:08,660 --> 00:29:09,640
It actually went up.

544
00:29:10,079 --> 00:29:11,200
It really went up.

545
00:29:13,539 --> 00:29:14,440
I'll leave it to you.

546
00:29:20,119 --> 00:29:21,160
Are you deaf?

547
00:29:23,359 --> 00:29:24,319
I'm sorry, Wan.

548
00:29:24,579 --> 00:29:26,079
I got a little carried away just now.

549
00:29:26,380 --> 00:29:27,799
But you have to admit, that move of yours

550
00:29:27,799 --> 00:29:29,240
was really a bit risky.

551
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:30,099
It was mostly just luck.

552
00:29:30,099 --> 00:29:31,200
Does it make a difference?

553
00:29:32,279 --> 00:29:33,240
I... I just mean...

554
00:29:33,339 --> 00:29:35,039
you need to be more careful next time.

555
00:29:36,359 --> 00:29:37,240
There won't be a next time.

556
00:29:37,900 --> 00:29:40,940
You made the company six million today, and then

557
00:29:41,039 --> 00:29:43,779
willingly gave up a year-end bonus of over half a million,

558
00:29:43,940 --> 00:29:44,500
and quit your job.

559
00:29:44,500 --> 00:29:45,440
You walked away from an

560
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:46,660
elite job on the 67th floor

561
00:29:46,700 --> 00:29:47,480
just to find a

562
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:49,059
crappy front-end developer like me on the 26th floor

563
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:51,279
to borrow 400,000 for crypto trading?

564
00:29:51,700 --> 00:29:52,640
I'm not borrowing.

565
00:29:52,980 --> 00:29:53,839
We're partnering up.

566
00:29:54,279 --> 00:29:55,799
We'll split the profits 50-50.

567
00:29:57,420 --> 00:29:59,400
You're completely sick in the head.

568
00:30:00,740 --> 00:30:01,200
Listen.

569
00:30:05,359 --> 00:30:06,720
The golden opportunity is right now.

570
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:08,880
Throw away that leash around your neck.

571
00:30:09,019 --> 00:30:10,000
Step out of here.

572
00:30:10,539 --> 00:30:12,000
Trust me. In two years,

573
00:30:12,259 --> 00:30:13,319
I guarantee you financial freedom.

574
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:14,920
It's not that I don't trust you.

575
00:30:15,859 --> 00:30:17,000
It's just that...

576
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:20,680
I'm getting married.

577
00:30:20,980 --> 00:30:21,680
Married?

578
00:30:21,880 --> 00:30:23,480
I met a girl.

579
00:30:23,579 --> 00:30:24,440
We've been dating for three months.

580
00:30:24,559 --> 00:30:25,799
After so many blind dates,

581
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:27,319
this is the first time I've met

582
00:30:27,799 --> 00:30:28,660
someone I click with so well.

583
00:30:28,700 --> 00:30:30,160
Really, it feels like a dream.

584
00:30:30,839 --> 00:30:32,019
She said getting married means

585
00:30:32,059 --> 00:30:33,240
I need to make a gesture.

586
00:30:33,420 --> 00:30:34,960
So I gave her all 400,000.

587
00:30:37,759 --> 00:30:38,960
You could buy 80,000 bowls of instant noodles

588
00:30:38,980 --> 00:30:40,180
and it wouldn't cost that much.

589
00:30:40,259 --> 00:30:40,880
You agreed?

590
00:30:40,960 --> 00:30:41,759
Of course.

591
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:44,039
A girl's youth is very precious, you know?

592
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:46,720
This money is just to give her a sense of security.

593
00:30:47,259 --> 00:30:48,240
Wang Zhiwu.

594
00:30:48,799 --> 00:30:50,440
I've known you for 20 years, right?

595
00:30:51,339 --> 00:30:53,759
You're a guy who mooches an egg off my noodles.

596
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:56,039
And now you're taking your hard-earned savings,

597
00:30:56,180 --> 00:30:56,960
getting on your knees,

598
00:30:57,099 --> 00:30:59,240
and giving it to a woman you've known for three months?

599
00:30:59,319 --> 00:31:00,000
You don't trust me,

600
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,700
but you believe money can buy love?

601
00:31:01,759 --> 00:31:02,759
So what if it's 20 years?

602
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,119
And what about three months?

603
00:31:04,259 --> 00:31:06,119
You're just being too extreme. I...

604
00:31:06,180 --> 00:31:07,920
I actually do trust her!

605
00:31:08,319 --> 00:31:09,000
I...

606
00:31:15,099 --> 00:31:16,039
Just wait.

607
00:31:19,579 --> 00:31:20,799
Back when it was at 3,000 dollars,

608
00:31:20,980 --> 00:31:21,839
they chickened out.

609
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:24,079
I turned around and threw everything in.

610
00:31:24,380 --> 00:31:25,839
When it hit 60,000,

611
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:27,680
they scrambled to get in.

612
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:29,079
I actually found it boring by then,

613
00:31:30,019 --> 00:31:31,240
so I dumped 30 percent of my position.

614
00:31:36,500 --> 00:31:37,680
It's just that over these past few years,

615
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:39,559
I hit a few key points right,

616
00:31:39,799 --> 00:31:40,980
and made some hard-earned money.

617
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:42,200
Two years.

618
00:31:42,619 --> 00:31:44,059
I suffered for two whole years

619
00:31:44,380 --> 00:31:45,400
to get some savings,

620
00:31:45,740 --> 00:31:47,000
planning to buy a house

621
00:31:47,740 --> 00:31:48,640
and get a wife.

622
00:31:51,440 --> 00:31:52,200
So...

623
00:31:53,559 --> 00:31:54,880
what about you now, Wan?

624
00:31:55,799 --> 00:31:56,759
I'm single.

625
00:31:57,960 --> 00:31:58,640
And you?

626
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:03,880
That depends on your

627
00:32:04,279 --> 00:32:05,680
performance today, Wan.

628
00:32:06,619 --> 00:32:07,480
Draft the contract.

629
00:32:07,980 --> 00:32:09,119
I'll take this house.

630
00:32:15,119 --> 00:32:15,960
What's wrong?

631
00:32:20,980 --> 00:32:22,480
You should show some performance too, right?

632
00:32:24,119 --> 00:32:24,680
Come on.

633
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:38,480
Okay.

634
00:32:39,339 --> 00:32:40,119
Hurry back.

635
00:32:54,079 --> 00:32:55,240
Wang Zhiwu

636
00:32:55,539 --> 00:32:57,519
So this is the love you bought

637
00:32:57,799 --> 00:33:00,000
with 400,000 yuan.

638
00:33:08,500 --> 00:33:09,680
How many times have I told you?

639
00:33:09,799 --> 00:33:11,720
Don't call me while I'm working!

640
00:33:22,640 --> 00:33:23,880
That childhood friend of mine...

641
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,200
got seriously ill.

642
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:26,480
He quit his job...

643
00:33:26,819 --> 00:33:28,519
and ended up flipping used bags.

644
00:33:28,660 --> 00:33:29,539
The funny thing is,

645
00:33:29,619 --> 00:33:30,799
he actually...

646
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,380
went to beg his wife for forgiveness.

647
00:33:34,900 --> 00:33:36,359
What's even funnier is...

648
00:33:36,759 --> 00:33:38,200
guess what his wife said.

649
00:33:39,220 --> 00:33:40,880
Just this once.

650
00:33:42,259 --> 00:33:44,000
That whole thing made me realize...

651
00:33:44,220 --> 00:33:46,799
some people are just beyond saving.

652
00:33:46,940 --> 00:33:49,279
That's just their fate.

653
00:33:50,920 --> 00:33:52,720
You guys are always preaching to me about...

654
00:33:52,839 --> 00:33:54,759
hard work and hope.

655
00:33:55,059 --> 00:33:56,000
In reality,

656
00:33:56,359 --> 00:33:57,380
you're just chasing the carrot

657
00:33:57,420 --> 00:33:59,680
someone else dangles in front of you.

658
00:33:59,880 --> 00:34:01,240
Or a cat chasing a laser pointer.

659
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:02,680
Burning your lives away,

660
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:04,180
just deluding yourselves.

661
00:34:04,859 --> 00:34:05,920
If you want to survive,

662
00:34:06,200 --> 00:34:07,599
you have to take a gamble.

663
00:34:07,660 --> 00:34:09,900
You have to pin those manipulators down,

664
00:34:09,940 --> 00:34:11,019
and beat them until they can't get up.

665
00:34:11,119 --> 00:34:12,159
Only then,

666
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:14,219
can you have a life like mine.

667
00:34:14,260 --> 00:34:15,059
Understand?

668
00:34:21,619 --> 00:34:23,239
Want to see what I'm capable of?

669
00:34:23,440 --> 00:34:25,440
I'm worried it'll keep you up at night.

670
00:34:25,820 --> 00:34:27,360
Let me put on some music for you.

671
00:34:27,500 --> 00:34:28,920
Are you ready? Come on,

672
00:34:29,820 --> 00:34:30,960
take a look.

673
00:34:33,059 --> 00:34:34,800
You only get one life.

674
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:36,460
I don't want to say much else.

675
00:34:37,539 --> 00:34:38,960
Fight hard,

676
00:34:39,219 --> 00:34:39,840
don't chicken out.

677
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:40,500
Don't be afraid.

678
00:34:40,559 --> 00:34:43,719
And don't leave yourselves any way out.

679
00:35:47,699 --> 00:35:49,199
Pack your things and head back.

680
00:36:11,659 --> 00:36:12,960
I warned you before,

681
00:36:13,579 --> 00:36:14,320
but you wouldn't listen.

682
00:36:15,500 --> 00:36:16,920
How much exactly did you lose this time?

683
00:36:19,559 --> 00:36:20,360
Ten million.

684
00:36:20,639 --> 00:36:26,199
Back to square one overnight.

685
00:36:29,219 --> 00:36:29,840
Maybe it's for the best.

686
00:36:31,519 --> 00:36:32,500
Consider it a lesson learned.

687
00:36:34,480 --> 00:36:35,920
We can just sell this house

688
00:36:36,239 --> 00:36:37,239
and get a smaller one.

689
00:36:37,460 --> 00:36:38,519
So every day when we're at home,

690
00:36:38,519 --> 00:36:39,800
we won't have to shout to be heard.

691
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:43,280
What are you laughing at?

692
00:36:44,119 --> 00:36:45,760
The house is gone.

693
00:36:46,719 --> 00:36:48,440
I put it all in.

694
00:37:18,860 --> 00:37:21,000
Mom and Dad recently bought a house.

695
00:37:21,139 --> 00:37:22,280
It might be a bit far,

696
00:37:22,460 --> 00:37:23,960
but the neighborhood is nice.

697
00:37:24,099 --> 00:37:26,719
Aren't you just asking to lose money buying a house now?

698
00:37:26,920 --> 00:37:27,800
I told you two a long time ago,

699
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,320
to let me manage your money.

700
00:37:29,659 --> 00:37:30,920
Why mess around like this?

701
00:37:31,119 --> 00:37:32,159
Well, we already bought it.

702
00:37:32,440 --> 00:37:33,440
It's for our retirement.

703
00:37:33,659 --> 00:37:35,599
You and An'an can live there for now.

704
00:37:35,940 --> 00:37:37,239
Then you won't need to rent anymore.

705
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:38,840
When did I ever need your charity?

706
00:37:38,940 --> 00:37:40,619
I'm just biding my time.

707
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:41,880
Let me tell you,

708
00:37:42,199 --> 00:37:43,199
let me tell you both,

709
00:37:43,500 --> 00:37:44,360
even if I starve to death,

710
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:45,880
I won't spend a single dime of yours.

711
00:37:46,099 --> 00:37:46,639
Three.

712
00:37:46,800 --> 00:37:47,400
Two.

713
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:48,119
One.

714
00:37:48,239 --> 00:37:50,039
Welcome home.

715
00:37:54,780 --> 00:37:56,760
The drywall has a minor leak.

716
00:37:57,139 --> 00:37:58,800
The baseboards are coming off in a few places.

717
00:37:59,239 --> 00:38:00,840
There are a few small cracks on the walls.

718
00:38:01,119 --> 00:38:02,559
Other than that, it's pretty good.

719
00:38:02,760 --> 00:38:04,119
It just needs some minor repairs.

720
00:38:06,079 --> 00:38:07,719
Our previous house was big, sure,

721
00:38:07,900 --> 00:38:09,719
but I never felt at ease there.

722
00:38:10,139 --> 00:38:11,920
It was like living in a general manager's office.

723
00:38:12,679 --> 00:38:14,119
This place is great.

724
00:38:14,519 --> 00:38:16,679
Once we decorate it together, it'll feel like a real home.

725
00:38:17,280 --> 00:38:18,880
Don't bother with all that.

726
00:38:19,320 --> 00:38:20,440
We're only staying for a bit anyway.

727
00:38:20,860 --> 00:38:21,800
I'm just waiting for the market to turn,

728
00:38:22,119 --> 00:38:23,320
then I'll bounce back in no time.

729
00:38:23,679 --> 00:38:25,119
What do you even have left to bounce back with?

730
00:38:32,099 --> 00:38:32,719
Thank you.

731
00:38:32,900 --> 00:38:33,800
Thank you for the guidance.

732
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:34,840
Everyone always says

733
00:38:35,119 --> 00:38:36,460
that my life is worthless.

734
00:38:36,699 --> 00:38:37,699
Just for reference.

735
00:38:37,820 --> 00:38:39,679
Your destiny is in your own hands.

736
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:51,659
Here,

737
00:38:52,440 --> 00:38:53,760
let me teach you a lesson first.

738
00:38:53,860 --> 00:38:55,440
This is called Cong Cai Ge.

739
00:38:55,659 --> 00:38:57,280
I'm not talking about massive wealth.

740
00:38:57,599 --> 00:38:58,019
At least...

741
00:38:58,019 --> 00:38:59,159
What do you want to ask me?

742
00:39:02,260 --> 00:39:03,199
I'm not asking.

743
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:04,960
I'm testing you.

744
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:07,519
I've had some minor setbacks lately.

745
00:39:07,619 --> 00:39:09,039
Just tell me the honest truth.

746
00:39:09,420 --> 00:39:11,239
See when I can turn things around.

747
00:39:12,900 --> 00:39:14,360
You bleed your parents dry,

748
00:39:14,360 --> 00:39:15,719
scheme for your wife's dowry,

749
00:39:15,719 --> 00:39:17,960
and later, perhaps even your child's

750
00:39:18,019 --> 00:39:19,380
lucky money will go to pay your debts.

751
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,800
Cong Cai, Cong Cai.

752
00:39:20,880 --> 00:39:22,699
It means following the root of gathering wealth,

753
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:24,760
not turning into a vicious dog.

754
00:39:25,079 --> 00:39:26,199
Your subsequent major fortune cycle

755
00:39:26,280 --> 00:39:27,679
shows no sign of life at all.

756
00:39:27,940 --> 00:39:29,960
I don't collect a fortune-telling fee from the doomed.

757
00:39:30,460 --> 00:39:31,960
Watch yourself.

758
00:39:52,599 --> 00:39:53,440
Calculate it again.

759
00:39:53,719 --> 00:39:55,440
I dare you to say that again.

760
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:57,840
It'll be the same no matter how many times I say it.

761
00:39:58,119 --> 00:40:00,400
This... is your fate.

762
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:02,079
Move.

763
00:40:06,400 --> 00:40:07,320
Superstition.

764
00:40:11,179 --> 00:40:12,000
Fakes.

765
00:40:12,519 --> 00:40:13,360
Wang Zhiwu.

766
00:40:13,840 --> 00:40:15,199
Can you stop messing with me?

767
00:40:15,260 --> 00:40:17,320
There are a lot of knockoffs of these couture pieces.

768
00:40:17,519 --> 00:40:19,519
The ones you brought are pretty good fakes,

769
00:40:19,860 --> 00:40:21,760
but if you know the details, they're obviously fake.

770
00:40:22,119 --> 00:40:22,860
Bullshit.

771
00:40:23,380 --> 00:40:24,260
The money she spent on the bags

772
00:40:24,340 --> 00:40:26,599
was what I transferred to her every year for her birthday.

773
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:29,119
Couldn't she have used the money for something else?

774
00:40:29,380 --> 00:40:30,400
You said it yourself.

775
00:40:30,980 --> 00:40:33,519
Did you think money could buy love?

776
00:40:42,920 --> 00:40:44,079
No smoking here.

777
00:40:44,780 --> 00:40:45,760
I'm not smoking.

778
00:40:46,159 --> 00:40:47,000
I'm selling this.

779
00:40:48,699 --> 00:40:50,199
What's going on with you lately?

780
00:40:50,599 --> 00:40:51,880
If you're short on cash, just ask.

781
00:40:52,719 --> 00:40:53,760
Me, short on cash?

782
00:40:56,360 --> 00:40:58,320
I'm just moving and clearing out some junk.

783
00:40:58,940 --> 00:41:00,800
This is a niche designer piece.

784
00:41:01,300 --> 00:41:02,800
Bought it for tens of thousands back in the day.

785
00:41:03,179 --> 00:41:04,920
Take a look. How much can I get for it?

786
00:41:05,099 --> 00:41:06,260
Some things

787
00:41:06,559 --> 00:41:08,599
might be all the rage for a while,

788
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:10,199
but once their time has passed,

789
00:41:10,300 --> 00:41:12,340
they're completely worthless.

790
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:14,519
Fine.

791
00:41:15,119 --> 00:41:15,760
Fine.

792
00:41:29,219 --> 00:41:30,039
Just you wait.

793
00:41:30,260 --> 00:41:30,880
Dai'er.

794
00:41:40,659 --> 00:41:41,860
What are you doing?

795
00:41:47,719 --> 00:41:49,500
You're acting crazy again, aren't you?

796
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:51,719
Where are you?

797
00:41:52,780 --> 00:41:54,159
Do you know what time it is?

798
00:41:54,579 --> 00:41:55,599
I'm working.

799
00:41:55,840 --> 00:41:56,960
Can you stop acting up?

800
00:41:57,519 --> 00:41:59,159
Now you're playing the saint?

801
00:41:59,980 --> 00:42:01,599
Bai An'an, I'm warning you.

802
00:42:02,340 --> 00:42:03,840
I'm giving you one hour

803
00:42:03,880 --> 00:42:05,199
to get back home.

804
00:42:05,820 --> 00:42:06,960
I have questions for you.

805
00:42:17,239 --> 00:42:19,039
I've been keeping count for you.

806
00:42:19,360 --> 00:42:20,599
Eight glasses in total.

807
00:42:20,900 --> 00:42:22,719
Three more to go.

808
00:42:22,940 --> 00:42:23,800
Finish them and I'll sign.

809
00:42:24,219 --> 00:42:25,019
I won't go back on my word.

810
00:42:26,619 --> 00:42:28,159
First glass.

811
00:42:28,519 --> 00:42:29,760
First glass.

812
00:42:29,820 --> 00:42:31,360
Good.

813
00:42:31,860 --> 00:42:32,420
The drink, the drink.

814
00:42:32,420 --> 00:42:33,599
Drink this. Drink this.

815
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:35,280
Second glass.

816
00:42:35,559 --> 00:42:36,800
Second glass.

817
00:42:36,860 --> 00:42:38,460
Okay.

818
00:42:41,039 --> 00:42:41,519
Here.

819
00:42:41,780 --> 00:42:42,480
Wait.

820
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:44,800
Third glass.

821
00:42:45,079 --> 00:42:46,800
Let's link arms for this one.

822
00:42:47,219 --> 00:42:48,000
Mr. Wang.

823
00:42:48,480 --> 00:42:49,599
We've been friends for years.

824
00:42:49,659 --> 00:42:50,559
Don't be so cheesy.

825
00:42:50,559 --> 00:42:51,760
You're... It's not cheesy.

826
00:42:51,760 --> 00:42:52,519
Let me toast you.

827
00:42:55,260 --> 00:42:56,199
Mr. Wang, is it?

828
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:57,840
Who are you?

829
00:42:58,079 --> 00:42:59,079
Let me toast you.

830
00:43:12,679 --> 00:43:14,280
You think you're a hero, huh?

831
00:43:14,639 --> 00:43:16,480
Throwing punches makes you a real man, right?

832
00:43:18,539 --> 00:43:19,880
Wan Fenqi, let me tell you.

833
00:43:20,440 --> 00:43:21,840
If I had known back then

834
00:43:22,019 --> 00:43:23,219
that you were so immature,

835
00:43:23,219 --> 00:43:25,239
I never would've married you.

836
00:43:26,019 --> 00:43:27,639
If you really cared about me,

837
00:43:27,719 --> 00:43:28,800
you wouldn't spend all day

838
00:43:28,920 --> 00:43:30,500
idling around and being so insecure.

839
00:43:30,500 --> 00:43:32,440
Don't make me look down on you.

840
00:43:34,039 --> 00:43:35,159
Let's just go home first. Come on.

841
00:43:37,519 --> 00:43:38,480
Don't hold me back!

842
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:39,079
Mr. Wang!

843
00:43:39,119 --> 00:43:40,480
I don't care who he is!

844
00:43:41,179 --> 00:43:42,099
What do you mean he has it hard?

845
00:43:42,199 --> 00:43:42,780
Stop right there!

846
00:43:43,800 --> 00:43:44,800
I'll smash your head in!

847
00:43:51,940 --> 00:43:52,559
Wan!

848
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:53,679
Wan!

849
00:43:53,960 --> 00:43:54,840
No, no, no! Wan!

850
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:55,960
Calm down! Calm down!

851
00:43:56,019 --> 00:43:57,159
Wan! Wan!

852
00:43:57,699 --> 00:43:58,159
Wan!

853
00:43:58,199 --> 00:43:59,460
Wan Fenqi!

854
00:44:04,760 --> 00:44:05,800
She backed out.

855
00:44:08,500 --> 00:44:09,960
Do you have any idea, from that client,

856
00:44:10,340 --> 00:44:11,800
how much commission I could've made?

857
00:44:12,400 --> 00:44:13,960
He was about to sign the deal!

858
00:44:15,599 --> 00:44:17,139
Could you stop being so extreme?

859
00:44:17,460 --> 00:44:19,559
You know exactly what that bastard was after!

860
00:44:20,500 --> 00:44:21,519
It's not like you didn't know.

861
00:44:22,019 --> 00:44:23,280
You were deliberately leading him on!

862
00:44:32,179 --> 00:44:33,800
When you're at the club with women in your arms,

863
00:44:33,880 --> 00:44:35,159
it's "talking business."

864
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:39,440
But my normal networking is "leading him on"?

865
00:44:40,679 --> 00:44:41,559
Wan Fenqi!

866
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:43,840
Don't be so fragile.

867
00:44:44,199 --> 00:44:46,159
There's no shame in your wife supporting you.

868
00:44:47,619 --> 00:44:48,559
You support me?

869
00:44:49,880 --> 00:44:52,360
The pennies you make are just a drop in the bucket!

870
00:44:53,559 --> 00:44:55,199
A junior college grad selling insurance.

871
00:44:55,260 --> 00:44:56,800
Without me, you'd still be in a shared apartment!

872
00:44:56,880 --> 00:44:57,440
A shared apartment?!

873
00:44:57,500 --> 00:44:59,360
What's wrong with a shared apartment?

874
00:45:00,460 --> 00:45:01,360
Right.

875
00:45:01,500 --> 00:45:02,840
How could it compare to this kind of

876
00:45:02,840 --> 00:45:04,400
godforsaken neighborhood?

877
00:45:04,980 --> 00:45:06,400
It takes half a year to fix the main road.

878
00:45:06,480 --> 00:45:07,960
I have to walk home on a dirt path every day.

879
00:45:08,079 --> 00:45:09,460
And enjoy the "rustic scenery" too.

880
00:45:09,460 --> 00:45:10,679
If you don't like it here, then get out!

881
00:45:10,739 --> 00:45:11,760
Get out and find your next guy!

882
00:45:11,840 --> 00:45:12,840
Fine, I'll get out!

883
00:45:13,019 --> 00:45:14,079
Then stop the car!

884
00:46:05,599 --> 00:46:06,519
Bai An'an

885
00:46:06,980 --> 00:46:07,960
Where are you?

886
00:46:08,340 --> 00:46:11,500
Hello, the number you dialed is powered off.

887
00:46:11,599 --> 00:46:13,599
Sorry, the number you...

888
00:46:20,960 --> 00:46:21,699
Wang Yi

889
00:46:22,559 --> 00:46:24,119
How old are you two? Still playing these games?

890
00:46:24,199 --> 00:46:25,079
Tell her to come up right now.

891
00:46:25,320 --> 00:46:26,460
She didn't go to my place.

892
00:46:26,519 --> 00:46:27,679
I'm actually here looking for her.

893
00:46:27,920 --> 00:46:29,000
Lao Liu from her department...

894
00:46:29,000 --> 00:46:30,179
...came looking for me today.

895
00:46:30,260 --> 00:46:32,000
Asking if she's really not coming to work anymore.

896
00:46:32,119 --> 00:46:34,159
She's not answering calls or replying on WeChat.

897
00:46:34,599 --> 00:46:35,599
What happened between you two?

898
00:46:36,639 --> 00:46:37,320
Lao Liu said...

899
00:46:37,380 --> 00:46:38,960
...you two had a terrible fight yesterday.

900
00:46:39,139 --> 00:46:40,199
Sounded like you're getting a divorce.

901
00:46:40,579 --> 00:46:41,840
Who's getting a divorce?

902
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:45,519
I went to pick her up yesterday.

903
00:46:46,139 --> 00:46:47,360
I pushed open the private room's door...

904
00:46:47,440 --> 00:46:48,679
...and it was a complete cesspool inside.

905
00:46:48,739 --> 00:46:49,360
Full of fat, sleazy guys.

906
00:46:49,420 --> 00:46:49,960
What was she trying to do?

907
00:46:50,019 --> 00:46:51,500
That's basically pimping her out, you know?

908
00:46:51,599 --> 00:46:52,539
Would you be okay with that?

909
00:46:52,619 --> 00:46:54,679
Tell me clearly first. What exactly happened?

910
00:46:56,960 --> 00:46:59,000
We had a fight on the way home.

911
00:46:59,119 --> 00:47:00,559
She just pushed the car door open and got out.

912
00:47:01,019 --> 00:47:01,880
I can't reach her.

913
00:47:02,420 --> 00:47:04,840
She didn't go home, and hasn't contacted me.

914
00:47:06,980 --> 00:47:08,000
Tell me the truth.

915
00:47:08,659 --> 00:47:10,559
Is she seeing someone else?

916
00:47:11,340 --> 00:47:13,480
No, absolutely not.

917
00:47:13,900 --> 00:47:15,800
She must've been so mad she went to her parents'.

918
00:47:17,739 --> 00:47:18,599
I'll go find her.

919
00:47:19,260 --> 00:47:20,760
Just calm down first.

920
00:47:21,039 --> 00:47:22,880
It's no use going there in this state.

921
00:47:23,179 --> 00:47:23,800
How about this.

922
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:25,800
I'll let Lao Liu at the company know first...

923
00:47:25,800 --> 00:47:26,719
...and ask for some time off for her.

924
00:47:26,840 --> 00:47:27,760
Once there's news about her...

925
00:47:27,820 --> 00:47:28,880
...make sure she contacts me.

926
00:47:41,099 --> 00:47:44,219
Hello. The number you have dialed is powered off.

927
00:47:44,420 --> 00:47:48,199
Sorry. The number you have dialed is powered off.

928
00:48:06,480 --> 00:48:07,280
An'an.

929
00:48:10,300 --> 00:48:11,039
Fenqi.

930
00:48:14,579 --> 00:48:15,239
Coming.

931
00:48:17,039 --> 00:48:17,940
Dad, why are you...

932
00:48:17,980 --> 00:48:19,619
Why didn't either of you answer my calls?

933
00:48:20,940 --> 00:48:21,840
You called?

934
00:48:22,059 --> 00:48:23,320
An'an, sorry to intrude.

935
00:48:23,760 --> 00:48:24,519
An'an?

936
00:48:27,440 --> 00:48:28,239
Where's An'an?

937
00:48:29,440 --> 00:48:30,400
Didn't she come home?

938
00:48:30,760 --> 00:48:31,480
Home?

939
00:48:32,280 --> 00:48:33,880
I texted her yesterday, and she didn't reply.

940
00:48:33,960 --> 00:48:35,159
I called, but her phone was off.

941
00:48:35,260 --> 00:48:36,920
The construction site I'm working on is right nearby.

942
00:48:37,219 --> 00:48:38,239
So I dropped by to check in.

943
00:48:38,539 --> 00:48:39,239
Where is she?

944
00:48:41,039 --> 00:48:42,599
We had a fight.

945
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:44,199
She got out of the car and left.

946
00:48:45,559 --> 00:48:46,840
Did you hit her again?

947
00:48:47,139 --> 00:48:47,780
I didn't.

948
00:48:47,780 --> 00:48:49,880
Last time was just an accident too.

949
00:48:50,039 --> 00:48:52,000
Call her back here. I'll ask her myself.

950
00:48:52,980 --> 00:48:54,280
I can't reach her.

951
00:49:05,480 --> 00:49:06,199
How many days has it been?

952
00:49:07,880 --> 00:49:09,079
It's been a week.

953
00:49:09,239 --> 00:49:10,760
A whole week.

954
00:49:12,679 --> 00:49:14,280
Dad, I keep calling her.

955
00:49:14,440 --> 00:49:15,559
And sending a dozen texts a day.

956
00:49:15,559 --> 00:49:16,559
She just won't reply.

957
00:49:16,739 --> 00:49:17,840
She must still be mad at me.

958
00:49:18,000 --> 00:49:19,059
Don't worry, I...

959
00:49:19,099 --> 00:49:20,559
You haven't looked for her in seven days,

960
00:49:21,179 --> 00:49:22,320
and you're still sleeping at home!

961
00:49:22,420 --> 00:49:23,000
Get up! No...

962
00:49:23,139 --> 00:49:23,380
Dad!

963
00:49:23,380 --> 00:49:23,920
Come with me.

964
00:49:24,119 --> 00:49:24,800
To the police station.

965
00:49:25,980 --> 00:49:27,000
Wan Fenqi!

966
00:49:27,099 --> 00:49:28,039
Speak!

967
00:49:28,119 --> 00:49:29,460
What did you do to my daughter?

968
00:49:29,460 --> 00:49:30,000
Sit down!

969
00:49:30,139 --> 00:49:30,699
Sit down!

970
00:49:31,079 --> 00:49:31,900
Calm down.

971
00:49:32,320 --> 00:49:33,860
We already understand the situation.

972
00:49:34,320 --> 00:49:35,099
This animal has laid hands

973
00:49:35,099 --> 00:49:36,440
on my daughter before.

974
00:49:36,559 --> 00:49:38,300
He's capable of anything.

975
00:49:38,400 --> 00:49:39,000
I suspect

976
00:49:39,059 --> 00:49:40,440
he's already killed my daughter.

977
00:49:40,539 --> 00:49:42,280
Wan Fenqi, tell me!

978
00:49:44,559 --> 00:49:45,480
Tell me right now!

979
00:49:45,900 --> 00:49:47,400
What did you do to my daughter?

980
00:49:47,840 --> 00:49:48,800
Wan Fenqi!

981
00:49:58,519 --> 00:49:59,280
Don't move!

982
00:50:00,539 --> 00:50:01,639
I told you not to move!

983
00:50:05,800 --> 00:50:07,519
Evidence collection at your house is done.

984
00:50:07,800 --> 00:50:09,239
If there's any news about your wife,

985
00:50:09,360 --> 00:50:10,840
we'll let you know immediately.

986
00:50:11,599 --> 00:50:12,360
Thank you.

987
00:50:12,840 --> 00:50:13,800
I won't see you out.

988
00:50:15,460 --> 00:50:16,320
Officer! Officer!

989
00:50:16,579 --> 00:50:17,880
What happened in there?

990
00:50:18,039 --> 00:50:18,960
Just a routine investigation.

991
00:50:19,139 --> 00:50:19,840
Nothing to worry about.

992
00:50:21,559 --> 00:50:22,440
Everyone, please clear out.

993
00:50:22,860 --> 00:50:23,480
Clear out.

994
00:50:27,000 --> 00:50:29,440
I told you not to move.

995
00:50:31,139 --> 00:50:32,340
Where are you going?

996
00:50:33,900 --> 00:50:35,119
Staying at my house...

997
00:50:35,940 --> 00:50:37,199
isn't it nice?

998
00:50:37,719 --> 00:50:38,880
Notice of Case Registration.

999
00:50:45,820 --> 00:50:46,840
This one, this one.

1000
00:50:49,480 --> 00:50:50,440
So,

1001
00:50:50,699 --> 00:50:52,360
all those packages of yours

1002
00:50:52,840 --> 00:50:54,679
were for the dog?

1003
00:50:55,519 --> 00:50:56,320
Yes.

1004
00:50:59,880 --> 00:51:01,159
Have you ever had a dog?

1005
00:51:01,579 --> 00:51:03,039
It smells so bad.

1006
00:51:04,039 --> 00:51:06,239
I was afraid it would pee everywhere,

1007
00:51:06,440 --> 00:51:08,679
so I bought it a collar online.

1008
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:10,880
Who knew I bought the wrong one?

1009
00:51:11,460 --> 00:51:13,079
My wife really likes dogs.

1010
00:51:14,239 --> 00:51:15,719
But I never took it seriously before.

1011
00:51:16,280 --> 00:51:17,719
Now I'm keeping it.

1012
00:51:18,239 --> 00:51:19,440
I figured,

1013
00:51:19,840 --> 00:51:21,440
if my wife comes back one day,

1014
00:51:21,679 --> 00:51:22,519
sees it,

1015
00:51:23,059 --> 00:51:24,039
and her heart softens,

1016
00:51:24,800 --> 00:51:25,880
she'll forgive me.

1017
00:51:27,139 --> 00:51:28,800
Actually, about this whole thing,

1018
00:51:29,300 --> 00:51:30,559
I never even thought

1019
00:51:30,599 --> 00:51:32,480
it had anything to do with your husband, Ma Dou.

1020
00:51:34,980 --> 00:51:36,599
Until the middle of that night.

1021
00:51:37,019 --> 00:51:37,880
I said, "Bro,

1022
00:51:38,420 --> 00:51:39,639
can you hurry up?

1023
00:51:39,940 --> 00:51:41,280
It's 11:30.

1024
00:51:42,539 --> 00:51:43,900
Are you made of pee?"

1025
00:51:52,599 --> 00:51:54,719
That was the tenth day of my wife's disappearance.

1026
00:51:55,340 --> 00:51:56,760
You hadn't returned from your hometown yet.

1027
00:52:17,059 --> 00:52:19,119
You... You startled me!

1028
00:52:19,699 --> 00:52:21,440
I never noticed before.

1029
00:52:21,719 --> 00:52:23,559
Noticed what?

1030
00:52:23,900 --> 00:52:24,960
Didn't notice...

1031
00:52:25,920 --> 00:52:27,320
that you're a night owl too.

1032
00:52:27,579 --> 00:52:28,400
I couldn't sleep.

1033
00:52:28,699 --> 00:52:29,880
So I wanted to find something to do.

1034
00:52:29,960 --> 00:52:31,599
And now you're even more awake, right?

1035
00:52:38,739 --> 00:52:41,039
Did... did you need me for something?

1036
00:52:41,760 --> 00:52:42,960
Nothing, I...

1037
00:52:43,760 --> 00:52:44,800
was just walking my dog.

1038
00:52:47,019 --> 00:52:47,840
Where's the dog?

1039
00:52:50,539 --> 00:52:51,719
Where did it run off to? The dog.

1040
00:52:51,920 --> 00:52:52,980
Alright, you keep looking.

1041
00:52:53,039 --> 00:52:53,880
I'll be going now.

1042
00:52:53,940 --> 00:52:54,559
Okay.

1043
00:53:10,900 --> 00:53:11,960
These earrings...

1044
00:53:12,519 --> 00:53:14,320
are exactly like the ones my wife wore

1045
00:53:14,579 --> 00:53:15,440
the day she went missing.

1046
00:53:21,679 --> 00:53:22,840
Ever since then,

1047
00:53:23,260 --> 00:53:24,920
I bought a video doorbell.

1048
00:53:32,260 --> 00:53:33,059
Here, let me help you.

1049
00:53:33,119 --> 00:53:33,840
No, it's fine.

1050
00:53:34,559 --> 00:53:35,800
Thanks. Thank you so much.

1051
00:53:35,920 --> 00:53:38,880
I overheard you on the phone before.

1052
00:53:39,179 --> 00:53:40,320
You said you were

1053
00:53:40,440 --> 00:53:42,719
coming back a few months after your postpartum recovery.

1054
00:53:42,980 --> 00:53:45,340
I figured your body would be mostly recovered by then.

1055
00:53:45,420 --> 00:53:46,960
But your husband, Ma Du,

1056
00:53:47,159 --> 00:53:49,880
bought a whole box of disposable underwear.

1057
00:53:50,179 --> 00:53:51,159
"Your wife is back."

1058
00:53:51,760 --> 00:53:52,519
"Thanks."

1059
00:53:54,500 --> 00:53:55,559
Who did he buy them for?

1060
00:53:56,559 --> 00:53:57,760
When you got back from your hometown,

1061
00:53:58,079 --> 00:53:59,920
I immediately went to check your size.

1062
00:54:01,820 --> 00:54:03,039
Your underwear

1063
00:54:03,460 --> 00:54:05,059
is size XL.

1064
00:54:06,039 --> 00:54:07,199
But the ones he bought

1065
00:54:07,420 --> 00:54:09,500
are size M.

1066
00:54:12,500 --> 00:54:13,619
After you came back,

1067
00:54:13,860 --> 00:54:15,800
I checked the video doorbell records every day.

1068
00:54:15,940 --> 00:54:17,199
I even checked them in the middle of the night.

1069
00:54:17,480 --> 00:54:18,400
Aside from the two of you,

1070
00:54:18,480 --> 00:54:19,800
no one else came in or out.

1071
00:54:22,059 --> 00:54:23,079
I was thinking,

1072
00:54:23,420 --> 00:54:24,900
am I just being too anxious?

1073
00:54:24,960 --> 00:54:26,400
Everyone looks like a thief to me.

1074
00:54:26,780 --> 00:54:28,719
But something still felt off.

1075
00:54:31,119 --> 00:54:32,400
So I followed Ma Du,

1076
00:54:32,780 --> 00:54:34,440
to see if I could find anything out.

1077
00:54:35,960 --> 00:54:36,679
And as a result,

1078
00:54:37,699 --> 00:54:39,280
he really gave himself away.

1079
00:54:39,440 --> 00:54:41,079
Please give me two large bags.

1080
00:54:41,460 --> 00:54:42,500
One is enough for these.

1081
00:54:42,500 --> 00:54:43,539
I'll have to charge you for two.

1082
00:54:43,539 --> 00:54:45,119
That's fine. Just give me two.

1083
00:54:45,880 --> 00:54:47,179
I saw with my own eyes

1084
00:54:47,360 --> 00:54:49,320
that he bought two of everything,

1085
00:54:49,639 --> 00:54:51,519
and put them into two separate bags.

1086
00:54:52,199 --> 00:54:53,920
If one bag was for you at home,

1087
00:54:54,179 --> 00:54:55,199
then the other bag...

1088
00:54:56,039 --> 00:54:58,599
who did he buy it for?

1089
00:55:00,039 --> 00:55:01,920
Are you asking me a question,

1090
00:55:02,079 --> 00:55:03,199
or are you

1091
00:55:03,840 --> 00:55:06,159
just trying to build suspense?

1092
00:55:06,840 --> 00:55:08,039
Don't waste my time.

1093
00:55:08,139 --> 00:55:09,119
Just spit it out.

1094
00:55:09,599 --> 00:55:11,519
Of course I'm asking you.

1095
00:55:11,780 --> 00:55:14,000
Why else would I knock on your door in the middle of the night?

1096
00:55:14,840 --> 00:55:16,880
I kept thinking you were in the dark.

1097
00:55:17,199 --> 00:55:18,039
So,

1098
00:55:18,639 --> 00:55:21,039
I checked the hospital's public shift schedule earlier,

1099
00:55:21,679 --> 00:55:23,280
found a day Ma Du was on duty,

1100
00:55:23,519 --> 00:55:24,880
and after confirming he wasn't home...

1101
00:55:25,039 --> 00:55:25,800
Ma Du!

1102
00:55:26,260 --> 00:55:28,079
I wanted to talk to you alone.

1103
00:55:28,400 --> 00:55:30,280
But you overreacted.

1104
00:55:30,460 --> 00:55:32,039
You didn't even give me a chance.

1105
00:55:32,800 --> 00:55:33,519
If you don't leave right now,

1106
00:55:33,699 --> 00:55:34,760
I'm calling the cops.

1107
00:55:40,539 --> 00:55:41,880
Is the owner of 102 here?

1108
00:55:42,139 --> 00:55:42,880
Who is it?

1109
00:55:48,179 --> 00:55:49,880
Is the owner of 102 at home?

1110
00:56:01,340 --> 00:56:02,000
What?

1111
00:56:02,239 --> 00:56:04,599
You can't leave things in the fire escape.

1112
00:56:04,820 --> 00:56:05,920
They do inspections.

1113
00:56:06,239 --> 00:56:07,360
You left this here, right?

1114
00:56:07,760 --> 00:56:09,559
Did you see me put it here with your own eyes?

1115
00:56:10,500 --> 00:56:11,900
Maybe 101 left it.

1116
00:56:12,059 --> 00:56:13,159
Sorry about that.

1117
00:56:13,360 --> 00:56:15,400
It was clean here yesterday.

1118
00:56:15,579 --> 00:56:16,340
How did it get so...

1119
00:56:16,340 --> 00:56:18,679
Just collect the trash and shut up.

1120
00:56:22,519 --> 00:56:23,519
But little did I know,

1121
00:56:23,739 --> 00:56:25,119
just this morning,

1122
00:56:25,840 --> 00:56:27,800
I made an unexpected discovery.

1123
00:56:43,500 --> 00:56:45,519
I've really run out of options.

1124
00:56:45,599 --> 00:56:47,119
I don't want to give up this chance.

1125
00:56:47,239 --> 00:56:48,380
I have to come in and take a look.

1126
00:56:48,380 --> 00:56:49,960
To see if there are any clues about my wife.

1127
00:56:50,780 --> 00:56:51,920
I'm recording this video

1128
00:56:52,079 --> 00:56:54,099
to prove that this fire door

1129
00:56:54,099 --> 00:56:55,559
really wasn't locked.

1130
00:56:55,900 --> 00:56:57,119
I didn't break it.

1131
00:56:57,960 --> 00:56:58,559
Go ahead.

1132
00:56:58,920 --> 00:56:59,840
Go ahead and search.

1133
00:57:00,099 --> 00:57:01,880
See where she's hiding.

1134
00:57:02,260 --> 00:57:03,320
Since you put it that way,

1135
00:57:03,320 --> 00:57:04,760
she's definitely not here.

1136
00:57:04,840 --> 00:57:05,719
What do you mean?

1137
00:57:06,679 --> 00:57:08,039
I teamed up with my husband

1138
00:57:08,179 --> 00:57:09,320
to kidnap your wife?

1139
00:57:09,679 --> 00:57:10,940
I never said that.

1140
00:57:11,079 --> 00:57:12,000
I patiently

1141
00:57:12,059 --> 00:57:13,440
listened to you ramble on.

1142
00:57:13,579 --> 00:57:15,280
I don't think there's anything wrong with my husband.

1143
00:57:15,360 --> 00:57:16,679
But I do think you

1144
00:57:17,300 --> 00:57:18,639
are a real piece of work.

1145
00:57:18,820 --> 00:57:19,719
Scaling walls, breaking in,

1146
00:57:20,179 --> 00:57:21,119
stalking,

1147
00:57:21,639 --> 00:57:22,639
peeping in the middle of the night...

1148
00:57:23,079 --> 00:57:25,480
I'm already being generous by not calling the cops.

1149
00:57:25,579 --> 00:57:27,039
If you really think there's something wrong with Ma Du,

1150
00:57:27,280 --> 00:57:27,800
you...

1151
00:57:27,940 --> 00:57:29,400
Here, take this earring

1152
00:57:29,480 --> 00:57:30,679
and take it to the police station.

1153
00:57:30,820 --> 00:57:31,800
What are you doing now?

1154
00:57:31,880 --> 00:57:32,920
Playing detective?

1155
00:57:34,179 --> 00:57:35,400
All I can say is,

1156
00:57:35,960 --> 00:57:38,079
you still don't know your husband very well.

1157
00:57:38,519 --> 00:57:39,639
He's a doctor.

1158
00:57:40,000 --> 00:57:41,400
Cutting people open every day...

1159
00:57:41,480 --> 00:57:42,559
Think how repressed he must be.

1160
00:57:43,800 --> 00:57:44,599
Look,

1161
00:57:46,460 --> 00:57:47,960
from when you got pregnant till now,

1162
00:57:48,159 --> 00:57:49,079
it's been over a year, right?

1163
00:57:49,480 --> 00:57:50,340
Has he touched you?

1164
00:57:50,480 --> 00:57:51,440
Excuse me,

1165
00:57:51,900 --> 00:57:53,360
I've known him since middle school.

1166
00:57:53,420 --> 00:57:54,719
I know him better than you do.

1167
00:57:55,380 --> 00:57:56,360
Of course. Of course.

1168
00:57:58,480 --> 00:57:59,960
But how can you be sure

1169
00:58:00,400 --> 00:58:02,360
you know everything about him?

1170
00:58:04,539 --> 00:58:05,679
Humans are animals too.

1171
00:58:06,280 --> 00:58:07,260
It's education,

1172
00:58:07,659 --> 00:58:08,679
rules,

1173
00:58:09,119 --> 00:58:11,559
and all kinds of restrictions choking our necks

1174
00:58:12,159 --> 00:58:14,880
that slowly turn us into humans.

1175
00:58:15,119 --> 00:58:16,480
You're a kindergarten teacher.

1176
00:58:17,079 --> 00:58:18,800
You should know this better than I do, right?

1177
00:58:19,860 --> 00:58:22,159
The kinder someone is,

1178
00:58:22,780 --> 00:58:24,519
the more softly they speak,

1179
00:58:24,760 --> 00:58:26,679
the tighter the chokehold on their neck.

1180
00:58:27,579 --> 00:58:29,320
And breaking free from this leash

1181
00:58:29,900 --> 00:58:30,760
often

1182
00:58:31,099 --> 00:58:32,920
only takes an instant.

1183
00:58:36,519 --> 00:58:38,000
So I suspect that day,

1184
00:58:38,619 --> 00:58:40,440
your husband ran into my wife.

1185
00:58:43,139 --> 00:58:43,880
Hi.

1186
00:58:45,159 --> 00:58:45,840
Hello.

1187
00:58:46,119 --> 00:58:48,440
I live in 101.

1188
00:58:49,519 --> 00:58:50,719
101?

1189
00:58:50,860 --> 00:58:52,119
You live in 102, right?

1190
00:58:52,199 --> 00:58:53,599
We met on the day we got our keys.

1191
00:58:55,559 --> 00:58:58,039
Isn't your husband with you?

1192
00:58:59,840 --> 00:59:00,920
Don't bring him up. So annoying.

1193
00:59:02,280 --> 00:59:03,960
Could you take me somewhere

1194
00:59:04,679 --> 00:59:06,199
where it's easy to catch a cab?

1195
00:59:07,639 --> 00:59:08,320
Sure.

1196
00:59:11,760 --> 00:59:12,260
Thanks.

1197
00:59:12,300 --> 00:59:12,760
No problem.

1198
00:59:12,800 --> 00:59:13,760
Come on, get in.

1199
00:59:23,460 --> 00:59:24,320
Did you have a fight?

1200
00:59:27,960 --> 00:59:29,039
Put your seatbelt on.

1201
00:59:55,519 --> 00:59:56,400
Wake up.

1202
00:59:57,639 --> 00:59:58,719
Don't fall asleep.

1203
01:00:46,300 --> 01:00:47,360
What are you doing?

1204
01:00:50,059 --> 01:00:51,039
Stay back!

1205
01:00:51,679 --> 01:00:53,199
No, listen to me.

1206
01:00:54,639 --> 01:00:55,960
No, listen to me.

1207
01:01:05,099 --> 01:01:05,940
Let me explain.

1208
01:01:06,420 --> 01:01:07,719
It's not what you think.

1209
01:01:08,320 --> 01:01:10,360
I... I don't know what came over me just now.

1210
01:01:11,739 --> 01:01:12,599
Listen to me.

1211
01:01:13,579 --> 01:01:14,360
Could you just...

1212
01:01:14,639 --> 01:01:15,699
...forget about this?

1213
01:01:15,760 --> 01:01:16,239
Stay back!

1214
01:01:16,280 --> 01:01:17,280
I'll do anything you want.

1215
01:01:17,420 --> 01:01:18,480
Listen to me. Stay back!

1216
01:01:18,599 --> 01:01:19,440
Don't come any closer!

1217
01:01:19,519 --> 01:01:20,840
If you come any closer, I'll call the police!

1218
01:01:22,380 --> 01:01:23,199
No, no... You can't.

1219
01:01:23,280 --> 01:01:24,539
Don't call the police. Don't call the police.

1220
01:01:24,619 --> 01:01:25,579
Please, don't.

1221
01:01:25,659 --> 01:01:26,659
Help!

1222
01:01:26,860 --> 01:01:28,719
Don't scream "Help"! Don't scream!

1223
01:01:36,420 --> 01:01:37,360
Help!

1224
01:01:53,579 --> 01:01:54,199
Help!

1225
01:01:54,360 --> 01:01:55,039
Help!
